  "prefLabel": "Phy 302.05 Direct supervision",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Phy 302.05 “Direct supervision” means “direct supervision” as defined in RSA 328-A:2, IV, namely “that the physical therapist is physically present and immediately available for direction and supervision. The physical therapist will have direct contact with the patient/client during each visit that is defined as all encounters with a patient/client in a 24-hour period. Telecommunications does not meet the requirement of direct supervision.”\n\nSource. #9233, eff 8-22-08; ss by #10933, eff 9-18-15; ss by #12864, eff 9-10-19; ss by #14563, eff 6-20-26, EXPIRES: 6-20-36",
